ue of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2026 so far, March to April sat at 51% of normal and April to May at 62%. Grid 18212 has a preliminary August to September 2026 estimate of 65.3, an estimate from NOAA rain that RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ from. The wettest pair is July to August at 13.24 inches normal, and the driest is October to November at 6.32.</p>"}
